    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193503": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow-Future Interfaces Group",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Post Doctoral Fellow-Future Interfaces Group Carnegie Mellon University: School of Computer Science: HCII Location Pittsburgh, PA Open Date Sep 14, 2026 Deadline Sep 21, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description The Future Interfaces Group (FIGLAB) at Carnegie Mellon University invites applications for a Post Doctoral Fellow working under the direction of Professor Chris Harrison. FIGLAB develops new sensing and interaction technologies that expand how people interact with computers, devices, and the physical world. Our work spans human–computer interaction, novel sensing systems, ubiquitous computing, wearable and mobile devices, augmented and virtual reality, embedded systems, signal processing, and machine learning. We are especially interested in researchers who enjoy building technically ambitious systems while also investigating compelling applications and user experiences. The successful candidate will work closely with Professor Harrison and other members of FIGLAB to develop and evaluate new interactive technologies. Candidates may contribute to existing research efforts or propose a complementary research direction that aligns with the lab’s broader interests. Relevant areas include, but are not limited to: * Novel sensing and interaction techniques * Mobile, wearable, and ubiquitous computing * Augmented, mixed, and virtual reality * On-body and around-device interaction * Acoustic, radio-frequency, optical, electrical, and physiological sensing * Embedded hardware and interactive devices * Applied machine learning for sensing and interaction * Fabrication and prototyping of novel interfaces * Human-centered evaluation of emerging technologies Responsibilities The researcher will be expected to: * Lead the design, implementation, and evaluation of original research projects * Develop functional hardware and software prototypes * Conduct technical experiments and, where appropriate, human-subject studies * Publish research in leading HCI and related venues * Collaborate with FIGLAB students, faculty, and external research partners * Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers * Contribute to the intellectual and collaborative environment of the lab * Assist in preparing research proposals and project reports, as appropriate Qualifications Applicants should have: * A Ph.D. in human–computer interaction, computer science, electrical or computer engineering, mechanical engineering, design, or a closely related field by the start of the appointment; visiting-scholar candidates may hold an equivalent academic or professional research position * A strong record of research and publication * Demonstrated ability to independently develop and execute research projects * Excellent written and verbal communication skills * An interest in interdisciplinary, collaborative, and prototype-driven research Experience in one or more of the following would be particularly valuable: * Electronics and embedded systems * Signal processing * Machine learning * Computer vision or computational imaging * RF, acoustic, capacitive, optical, or physiological sensing * Mechanical design and digital fabrication * Mobile, wearable, XR, or interactive-system development * Experimental design and user studies Candidates are not expected to have experience in every area. We welcome applicants with complementary technical or methodological strengths who are interested in expanding into new areas. Applicants are encouraged to familiarize themselves with FIGLAB’s research before applying. A strong application will clearly explain how the candidate’s expertise could complement the lab’s current work and enable distinctive new research. Application Instructions Applications should include a cover letter describing qualifications, a CV and contact information for 3 references. Please direct questions and interest in the position to charriso@andrew.cmu.edu Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Carnegie Mellon University is an equal opportunity employer. It does not discriminate in admission, employment, or administration of its programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy or related condition, family status, marital status, parental status, religion, ancestry, veteran status, or genetic information. Furthermore, Carnegie Mellon University does not discriminate and is required not to discriminate in violation of federal, state, or local laws or executive orders. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List‎ Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List‎ Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"
